<title>CANADA: Toronto exchange to close trading floor April 23.</title>
<headline>Toronto exchange to close trading floor April 23.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Toronto Stock Exchange said on Tuesday it will close its trading floor on April 23 after it solved problems with its computer trading system.</p>
<p>The balance of floor-traded stocks will move to CATS (computer assisted trading system) beginning April 14, the exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;We have successfully identified and corrected a long-standing programming problem in CATS that was triggered by the unprecedented order flow in Bre-X (Minerals Ltd) shares,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
